<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ligurian Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1797–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ligurian Republic was a French client state that replaced the aristocratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> in 1797, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> pressed the old regime to give way to a democratic government. It covered Genoa and the Ligurian coast and was closely tied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the wars of the period. In 1805 it was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>, and after Napoleon's fall the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> gave its territory to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ligurian-republic.jpg" alt="Ligurian Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Genoa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
